1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:00,888
Wallet.

2
00:00:00,888 --> 00:00:01,526
Swap.

3
00:00:01,526 --> 00:00:02,165
Earn.

4
00:00:02,165 --> 00:00:02,803
Buy.

5
00:00:02,803 --> 00:00:06,632
One app, built on one toolkit.

6
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:13,645
Hi, I'm Emilio, your agent inside WDK, Tether's Wallet Development Kit.

7
00:00:13,645 --> 00:00:22,473
This is the WDK Starter Wallet: an open-source React Native app you can fork and make your own.

8
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:24,312
Here's the idea.

9
00:00:24,312 --> 00:00:30,519
Your app talks to WDK, and WDK runs in its own worklet on the device.

10
00:00:30,519 --> 00:00:34,244
That's where the keys live, and they never leave.

11
00:00:34,244 --> 00:00:38,797
Every chain and every protocol is a module you plug in.

12
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:40,705
Two phones.

13
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,651
On the left, a brand-new wallet.

14
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:48,302
Twelve words, generated on the device.

15
00:00:48,302 --> 00:00:51,355
We blurred them; never share yours.

16
00:00:51,948 --> 00:00:55,003
A password encrypts everything locally.

17
00:00:55,598 --> 00:01:00,317
Then back it up, encrypted, to Google Drive or iCloud.

18
00:01:00,317 --> 00:01:01,261
Your choice.

19
00:01:04,932 --> 00:01:10,194
On the right, an existing wallet, imported from its recovery phrase.

20
00:01:12,348 --> 00:01:18,299
The balance is already there: ninety-eight dollars and ninety cents, on testnet.

21
00:01:18,897 --> 00:01:23,007
Left phone: Receive, and copy the address.

22
00:01:24,897 --> 00:01:28,351
Right phone: send one USDT.

23
00:01:30,897 --> 00:01:33,363
Look at the fee.

24
00:01:33,363 --> 00:01:33,980
Free.

25
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:37,679
Gas is sponsored, thanks to EIP-7702.

26
00:01:38,277 --> 00:01:39,171
Sent.

27
00:01:42,277 --> 00:01:45,811
And both balances update, one dollar over.

28
00:01:46,407 --> 00:01:48,133
Now, on mainnet.

29
00:01:50,407 --> 00:01:53,669
Let's swap fifty POL for USDT.

30
00:01:54,265 --> 00:02:03,602
In Automatic mode I ask LI.FI, Symbiosis, 0x and Rhino.fi at once, and the best quote wins.

31
00:02:03,602 --> 00:02:05,800
This time, it's Symbiosis.

32
00:02:06,393 --> 00:02:09,336
Submitted, and the balances follow.

33
00:02:11,393 --> 00:02:14,132
Same screen, different chain.

34
00:02:14,132 --> 00:02:18,240
Fifteen USDT from Polygon to Ethereum.

35
00:02:18,842 --> 00:02:24,421
Zero-x only swaps on one chain, so it sits this one out.

36
00:02:24,421 --> 00:02:26,280
LI.FI takes the route.

37
00:02:26,882 --> 00:02:30,448
Fifteen USDT, now on Ethereum.

38
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:34,512
Idle USDT?

39
00:02:34,512 --> 00:02:36,437
Put it to work.

40
00:02:36,437 --> 00:02:39,805
These are Morpho vaults, with live APY.

41
00:02:40,398 --> 00:02:42,989
I'll deposit two USDT.

42
00:02:43,798 --> 00:02:50,021
You always see a summary first: approvals, if needed, and gas is sponsored.

43
00:02:52,048 --> 00:02:54,511
Withdrawing works the same way.

44
00:02:57,048 --> 00:03:02,807
And if you hold Tether Gold, you can use it as collateral to borrow USDT.

45
00:03:05,907 --> 00:03:07,335
Need more USDT?

46
00:03:07,335 --> 00:03:12,097
Pick an amount, in euros or dollars, and a network.

47
00:03:12,697 --> 00:03:17,623
Fifty dollars gets about forty-six sixty-five USDT.

48
00:03:18,225 --> 00:03:21,210
Transak handles payment and checks.

49
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:34,431
This demo runs on Transak's staging environment, so the purchase shows up right away.

50
00:03:35,028 --> 00:03:38,463
Wallet, swaps, yield and fiat, all self-custodial.

51
00:03:38,463 --> 00:03:43,859
Fork it, swap modules in or out, and ship your own.

52
00:03:43,859 --> 00:03:45,331
Build the wallet.

53
00:03:45,331 --> 00:03:46,803
Keep the keys.
